SUMMARY:SOLD OUT! Cyberdeck workshop: build your own 'mesh-berry' 🫐 #2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261107T120000Z
DTEND:20261107T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Hand-soldered cyberdecks are all over the internet. The cyberde
 cks we know from cyberpunk fiction and hacker culture were improvised mach
 ines—originally appearing in William Gibson’s 1984 novel Neuromancer
 —often built within a narrow and masculine idea of who gets to tinker\,
  hack\, and build. The cyberdecks filling our feeds today look different.
  They’re cute. \nFrom mermaid-shell Raspberry Pis to Hello Kitty makeup
  cases\, these devices have exploded in popularity over the past year\, th
 anks to women teaching each other to build artistic\, hyper-feminine compu
 ters online. \nCyberdecks push back against the sleek\, sealed\, and extra
 ctive technologies we rely on every day. While most consumer computers loc
 k us into systems that are becoming increasingly unethical\, from non-cons
 ensual surveillance to automatic AI integration no one asked for\, cyberde
 cks are hacked together. Often built with femininity and sustainability in
  mind\, they’re personalised with cute and colourful items that would ot
 herwise be thrown away. In an age of mass-produced devices\, cyberdecks tu
 rn technology into a form of self-expression. \nMake your personalised ‘
 mesh-berry’! 🫐\nIn this workshop\, you’ll build your very own\, per
 sonalised ‘mesh-berry’ 🫐 device: a local chat tool that runs on a m
 esh network. You don’t need WiFi\, internet\, or anything Big Tech relat
 ed. To keep things accessible\, we won’t build a full computer\, but foc
 us on a working chat tool you can actually take home and use\, change\, or
  build upon. \nGuided by web developer and artist Heerko van der Kooij\, y
 ou’ll learn how to hand-solder your own motherboard and how to style you
 r chat program. Lilian Stolk from The Hmm will go a bit deeper into the ae
 sthetic side of things\, looking at how (and why) to design a personal cas
 e for your device \nAfter the workshop\, you’ll walk away with a working
  mesh-berry that you can use to chat with other mesh-berry owners nearby.
  If your friends couldn’t make it to this workshop\, you’ll have picke
 d up the skills to build one for them yourself. \nRequirements and Prep\n\
 nYou don’t need to have any experience with coding to join this workshop
 . The ticket price includes all the hardware you’ll need: a screen\, key
 board\, battery\, and speaker. We’ll provide some basic crafting materia
 ls\, but we ask you to bring your own case that is at least 5x7cm (a bag\
 , box\, tin\, or anything else you’d like to turn into your device’s s
 hell) and extra bits and pieces to personalise it further. Think of sticke
 rs\, fabric\, beads\, paint\, or anything else that makes it yours. The wo
 rkshop will be conducted in English. Please feel free to join us\, but don
 ’t wait to long. Our first workshop sold out fast. \nSize hardware:\n–
  screen (including outside): 8\,5 x 5 x 1 cm (size of the screen is 6\,5 x
  4\,9 cm). It needs a bit of extra space for the battery\, the speaker and
  cables.\n– keyboard: 8\,4 x 5\,3 cm\nCheck for an image in the speaker
  carousel. \nThe Hmm experiments…\nThis event is part of a series of pro
 grams that we are developing with The Hmm\, where we give space in our stu
 dio for our community to explore new ideas and experiment with workshops a
 s part of our public program. \n\nWhat you need to know\n\n📅 Date: Satu
 rday 26 September 2026\n🕗 Times: 13.00 – 17.00 CEST\n📍 Location: T
 he Hmm’s studio\, NDSM-plein 125\, 1033 WC Amsterdam\n🎟 Tickets: €5
 5 regular\, €51\,50 students (this is including €47\,50 for hardware m
 aterial)\n\nAs these workshops are more intimate sessions\, there is a lim
 ited supply of tickets available. You can find information about physical
  accessibility at The Hmm’s studio here. \n\n💚 This programme is kind
 ly supported by the Creative Industries Fund NL
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/cyberdeck-workshop-build-your-own-mesh-berry-2/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
