SUMMARY:The Hmm TO the Chinese Internet
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261125T190000Z
DTEND:20261125T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:What does the Chinese internet look like from the inside?\n‎\
 nThe Hmm’s Chinese Internet Tour takes you on a guided trip through Chin
 a’s social media ecosystem\, led by media anthropologist Dino Ge Zhang w
 hose research focuses on emotions and relationships on live streaming plat
 forms in the Chinese-speaking world. \nWe’ll visit destinations like the
  face-filter app Meitu (美图公司) and the Myspace-like relic Qzone (QQ
 空间) to the TikTok-style short-video platform Kuaishou (快手)\, where
  artists\, researchers\, and designers with local expertise show us how th
 ese platforms work\, what makes them distinct\, and how to navigate the pr
 actical barriers to using them.\n‎\nWe often think of the social media p
 latforms we use in the West as global. Yet behind China’s Great Firewall
 \, a vast and largely separate social media ecosystem has developed\, with
  platforms that are used by hundreds of millions of people but remain rela
 tively unfamiliar outside the country. These platforms have their own cult
 ures and conventions\, shaped by China’s particular internet landscape.
  They are also spaces where new trends\, memes\, and visual languages emer
 ge\, many of which eventually make their way onto the global internet\, so
 metimes months or years later.\n‎\nFor people outside China\, getting a
  glimpse of these platforms means seeing the internet from a perspective t
 hat is rarely available. Many got their first glimpse of this world in Jan
 uary 2025\, when RedNote (小红书) surged in popularity after the US gov
 ernment threatened to ban TikTok. For a brief moment\, the platform became
  a possible refuge for TikTok users\, attracting a wave of curious newcome
 rs from outside China. But TikTok was only unavailable for about a day\, a
 nd most of these new users remained RedNote day-trippers.\n‎\nThe Hmm’
 s Chinese Internet Tour picks up where that moment left off. Moving beyond
  RedNote\, we’ll explore the wider landscape of platforms\, communities\
 , aesthetics\, and strange digital corners that make up China’s internet
 \, and get a sense of what it looks like from the inside.\n‎\nWhat you n
 eed to know\n‎ Guided by Dino Zhang\n\n\n📅 Date: Wednesday 25 Novembe
 r 2026\n🕗 Times: 20.00 – 21.30 CET\n📍 Location: The Inbetween\n
 🎟 Tickets: €5\n‎\n\n‎💚 This programme is kindly supported by t
 he Creative Industry Fund.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/the-hmm-to-the-chinese-internet/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
